Chimera's fix to the fork's Bink 2 decoder (wasm/bink2/build.sh applies it).

Alpha: frame flag 0x80000 means the frame carries no alpha data, and its whole
alpha plane is then one value, the frame flags' top byte (0 where an interface
piece starts blank, 255 through most of the intro, 17, 34 ... 238 in a fade).
The fork read an alpha plane from every frame of a movie with alpha, so each
frame with the flag failed and was dropped: 15 of the Remastered Collection's
80 movies with alpha set it, and six of those gave no frames at all (INTRO2
gave 762 of 3,283). With the flag the plane isn't
read or motion-compensated, just filled. Checked against frames exported with
alpha by RAD Video Tools (305 of them, from two movies): no pixel's alpha more
than 9 levels off. All 80 decode, each slice ending where its offset says.

The fill covers the whole decoded area, the size rounded up to 32 each way,
not only the picture: a later frame's motion compensation can read from below
the picture, which would otherwise be whatever the buffer held. Filling only
the picture made GDI1, INTRO2, LOGO and EARTH_E-00 come out differently on
FFmpeg 2022 and 7.1, from the leftover memory alone.

diff --git a/libavcodec/bink2.c b/libavcodec/bink2.c
index fe868f0..d20477a 100644
--- a/libavcodec/bink2.c
+++ b/libavcodec/bink2.c
@@ -310,6 +310,15 @@ static int bink2_decode_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *frame,
 
     skip_bits_long(gb, 32 + 32 * (c->num_slices - 1));
 
+    /* Frame flag 0x80000: the frame has no alpha data. Its alpha plane is one
+     * value throughout, the frame flags' top byte: 0 (transparent) where an
+     * interface piece starts blank, 255 (opaque) through most of the intro.
+     * The whole decoded area, 32-aligned, is filled: motion compensation in
+     * later frames reads the rows below the picture too. */
+    if (c->has_alpha && (c->frame_flags & 0x80000))
+        for (int y = 0; y < height_a; y++)
+            memset(frame->data[3] + y * frame->linesize[3], c->frame_flags >> 24, FFALIGN(avctx->width, 32));
+
     if (c->frame_flags & 0x10000) {
         if (!(c->frame_flags & 0x8000))
             bink2_get_block_flags(gb, 1, (((avctx->height + 15) & ~15) >> 3) - 1, c->row_cbp);
diff --git a/libavcodec/bink2g.c b/libavcodec/bink2g.c
